# Glide images

Import `{{ package }}.image.loadGlide` and call it on the main thread on an `ImageView` from ViewBinding or Compose `AndroidView`. Set the target view's size, scale type and content description for your layout.

```kotlin
binding.preview.loadGlide(url, placeholder = R.drawable.loading, error = R.drawable.unavailable)
```

The placeholder appears while loading. The error drawable covers request failures and null models. Both IDs are optional. Glide manages caching, lifecycle and replacement of requests on a reused target. Use `clearGlide()` when recycling a target without a new request or in Compose `AndroidView.onRelease`. In a Fragment, clear a request tied to its view before dropping the binding.

No Application initialization, Glide annotation processor or Compose integration artifact is needed. The Compose preset uses an Android `ImageView` through `AndroidView`.
